Hi Rosa,

Thank you both again for the discovery call last week - the picture of
where your in-house meter is undercounting and why finance has stopped
trusting the partner-billing numbers was exactly what I needed. Here is the
proposal we discussed.

Plan
- Scale plan: $4,500/mo, billed annually ($54,000/yr).
- Includes 75M events/mo, comfortably above your estimated 40-60M with
  headroom for vessel-schedule spikes.
- SSO (SAML) included at this tier.

Overage
- Usage above the 75M included volume is billed as overage.
- 5% grace threshold: any month that exceeds the included volume by 5% or
  less incurs no overage charge - so a normal spiky month won't surprise
  you. Exact per-1M overage rate is on the attached order form.

Onboarding plan (built around the dual-run we talked about)
- Weeks 1-2: integration. Wire your collector to our batch ingest (up to
  1,000 events/request) with idempotency keys, validate end to end.
- Weeks 3-14: dual-run and reconciliation. Your in-house pipeline stays
  live; we run in parallel and reconcile totals each period - ours against
  yours against your gateway logs - until the deltas are boring and
  explainable.
- Cutover: after one clean reconciled month, we retire the old pipeline and
  Acme becomes the system of record for partner billing.

I've attached our standard order form and MSA. A couple of things worth
flagging directly rather than burying: we're single-region today with
tested cross-region disaster recovery, so a regional event means downtime,
not seamless failover - I'd rather you have that in writing. Section 6.3 of
the MSA also covers fee disputes, which given your history with untrusted
numbers is worth Ben and your finance team reading.

To keep momentum, I'd like to book the technical deep-dive with one of our
platform engineers so Ben can go deep on ingest, dedup, and the
reconciliation workflow. I have slots the week of May 19 - reply with what
works and I'll send an invite.

Looking forward to it.

